<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>2026/10 on Sebastian Korotkiewicz - Tech{{log}}</title><link>https://sekor.eu.org/archive/2026/10/</link><description>Recent content in 2026/10 on Sebastian Korotkiewicz - Tech{{log}}</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:39:21 +0200</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://sekor.eu.org/archive/2026/10/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Push to multiple git remotes with one command</title><link>https://sekor.eu.org/note/push-to-multiple-git-remotes/</link><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:39:21 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://sekor.eu.org/note/push-to-multiple-git-remotes/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Push to multiple git remotes with one command&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I keep my main repo on a self-hosted server and mirror it to GitHub. Two remotes, one command.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Add the remotes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;git remote add aurcade ssh://git@myserver.org:2222/user/repo.git&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;git remote add github git@github.com:user/repo.git&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;git remote -v &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# check&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Add an alias&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;In &lt;code&gt;.git/config&lt;/code&gt; (this repo only) or &lt;code&gt;~/.gitconfig&lt;/code&gt; (all repos):&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-ini" data-lang="ini"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;[alias]&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;pushall&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#34;!git push aurcade &amp;amp;&amp;amp; git push github&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Now &lt;code&gt;git pushall&lt;/code&gt; pushes to both. The alias even shows up in tab completion.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>